I would expect an unimplemented type for cast error.

### What happens?

Running a sql query leads to JVM crash with exit status code 134. The query involves a nested query and is using `array_agg` function. Details to reproduce below.

### To Reproduce

I wrote the simple test class to reproduce the issue. The faulty query is this one:
```sql
select "___alias___portfolio_Ticker___", "___alias___portfolio_Portfolio___", count(*) as "_contributors_count_", array_agg("___alias___DateScenario_any_value___") as "VaR 95_1", max("___alias___grouping_portfolio_Portfolio___") as "___grouping______alias___portfolio_Portfolio______", array_agg("___alias___ScenarioValue_sum___") as "VaR 95_0", max("___alias___grouping_portfolio_Ticker___") as "___grouping______alias___portfolio_Ticker______" from (select "portfolio"."Portfolio" as "___alias___portfolio_Portfolio___", "portfolio"."DateScenario" as "___alias___portfolio_DateScenario___", "portfolio"."Ticker" as "___alias___portfolio_Ticker___", grouping("portfolio"."Portfolio") as "___alias___grouping_portfolio_Portfolio___", grouping("portfolio"."Ticker") as "___alias___grouping_portfolio_Ticker___", any_value("portfolio"."DateScenario") as "___alias___DateScenario_any_value___", sum("portfolio"."ScenarioValue") as "___alias___ScenarioValue_sum___" from "portfolio" group by grouping sets(("___alias___portfolio_DateScenario___"), ("___alias___portfolio_Ticker___","___alias___portfolio_Portfolio___","___alias___portfolio_DateScenario___"), ("___alias___portfolio_Ticker___","___alias___portfolio_DateScenario___"))) group by "___alias___portfolio_Ticker___", "___alias___portfolio_Portfolio___" limit 10001
```

Test class:
```java
import org.duckdb.DuckDBConnection;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.InputStream;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Path;
import java.nio.file.StandardCopyOption;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.ResultSet;
import java.sql.Statement;

public class TestDuckDBQueryCrash {
  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
    DuckDBConnection connection = createConnection();
    loadFile(connection, "portfolio.csv", "portfolio");

    try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
      ResultSet tableResult = statement.executeQuery("select * from portfolio limit 10");
      int c = 0;
      while (tableResult.next()) {
        c++;
      }
      System.out.println("First query, number of lines " + c);
    }
    String sql = """
            select "___alias___portfolio_Ticker___", "___alias___portfolio_Portfolio___", count(*) as "_contributors_count_", array_agg("___alias___DateScenario_any_value___") as "VaR 95_1", max("___alias___grouping_portfolio_Portfolio___") as "___grouping______alias___portfolio_Portfolio______", array_agg("___alias___ScenarioValue_sum___") as "VaR 95_0", max("___alias___grouping_portfolio_Ticker___") as "___grouping______alias___portfolio_Ticker______" from (select "portfolio"."Portfolio" as "___alias___portfolio_Portfolio___", "portfolio"."DateScenario" as "___alias___portfolio_DateScenario___", "portfolio"."Ticker" as "___alias___portfolio_Ticker___", grouping("portfolio"."Portfolio") as "___alias___grouping_portfolio_Portfolio___", grouping("portfolio"."Ticker") as "___alias___grouping_portfolio_Ticker___", any_value("portfolio"."DateScenario") as "___alias___DateScenario_any_value___", sum("portfolio"."ScenarioValue") as "___alias___ScenarioValue_sum___" from "portfolio" group by grouping sets(("___alias___portfolio_DateScenario___"), ("___alias___portfolio_Ticker___","___alias___portfolio_Portfolio___","___alias___portfolio_DateScenario___"), ("___alias___portfolio_Ticker___","___alias___portfolio_DateScenario___"))) group by "___alias___portfolio_Ticker___", "___alias___portfolio_Portfolio___" limit 10001
                        """;
    try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
      for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
        ResultSet tableResult = statement.executeQuery(sql);
        int c = 0;
        while (tableResult.next()) {
          c++;
        }
        System.out.println("Second query, number of lines " + c);
      }
    }
  }

  private static DuckDBConnection createConnection() {
    try {
      Class.forName("org.duckdb.DuckDBDriver");
      return (DuckDBConnection) DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:duckdb:");
    } catch (Exception e) {
      throw new RuntimeException(e);
    }
  }

  private static void loadFile(DuckDBConnection connection, String fileName, String table) {
    Path tempPath = null;
    try {
      InputStream in = Thread.currentThread().getContextClassLoader().getResourceAsStream(fileName);
      tempPath = Files.createTempFile(fileName + "_tmp_" + System.currentTimeMillis(), ".csv");
      Files.copy(in, tempPath, StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING); // copy the file in tmp dir. otherwise, issue can happen in docker container (file system does not exist)
      Statement statement = connection.createStatement();
      statement.execute("CREATE TABLE " + table + " AS SELECT * FROM read_csv_auto('" + tempPath + "');");
    } catch (Exception e) {
      throw new RuntimeException(e);
    } finally {
      if (tempPath != null) {
        try {
          Files.delete(tempPath);
        } catch (IOException e) {
          throw new RuntimeException(e);
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The data is loaded from the csv file attached here.
[portfolio.csv](https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/files/14386834/portfolio.csv)

Console output:
```
First query, number of lines 10

Process finished with exit code 134 (interrupted by signal 6:SIGABRT)
```

There is no exception raised nor core dump files after running this code. 


